          "kicker": "Provincial move",
          "heading": "Ciaran Frawley joins Connacht from Leinster to strengthen Ireland World Cup claims",
          "body": "Ireland international Ciaran Frawley has swapped Leinster for Connacht as the United Rugby Championship season begins, aiming to secure regular minutes ahead of the 2027 World Cup. Frawley is the marquee signing for Stuart Lancaster, who has also recruited former Leinster pair Will Connors and Jerry Cahir. Meanwhile, Leo Cullen begins his final season in charge of defending champions Leinster, who remain the \"team to beat\" according to 35-cap former international Simon Zebo as players look to impress Andy Farrell."
        }
