          "heading": "Darcy Graham Ruled Out Of Scotland Tests Following Severe Bicep Injury",
          "body": "Scotland and Edinburgh winger Darcy Graham faces a minimum of 12 weeks on the sidelines after rupturing his bicep during a recent friendly. The 29-year-old, who has scored 38 tries in 57 Tests, will miss the upcoming autumn series at Murrayfield. Edinburgh head coach Sean Everitt confirmed the news during his team announcement on Friday, noting the injury was a \"pretty freakish\" collision. The recovery timeline rules the talismanic flyer out of Scotland's November fixtures against New Zealand, Australia, and Japan."
